{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_b3kyr3qpmzxu3s2t233kfijedizrusgmvetsdj4hysfl4wstodia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. The rust-analyzer diagnostics about `u8 as c_void` are a false positive — `c_char` on Linux is `i8` (a primitive numeric type), so `b'=' as c_char` is a valid primitive cast. The real rustc compiler accepts the code (`cargo check` and `cargo build --release` both succeed).\n\nSummary:\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — declares `driver` library with `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, `libc` runtime dependency, and `libloading` dev dependency.\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — translates `c_src/src/lib.c`:\n  - `encode()` is a private helper preserving the C signed-char return.\n  - `encode_base64` is exported via `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"` with the matching signature `(c_int, *const c_char) -> *mut c_char`.\n  - Uses `libc::calloc` and `libc::strlen` so callers can `free()` the result, exactly like the C version.\n  - Preserves the original error-check order, the `size = 0 → strlen` fallback, the `(size * 4 / 3 + 4)` allocation, and the bit-twiddling for 6-bit groups.\n- **`tests/ffi_compare.rs`** — loads both `c_src/build/libdriver.so` and `target/release/libdriver.so` via `libloading`, calls `encode_base64` through the FFI boundary on both, frees the returned memory through `libc.so.6::free`, and asserts byte-identical output for: NULL input, empty string with size==0, common ASCII strings, every length 1–30 with patterned data, every single/double/triple byte value 0–255, and explicit-size variants. All 7 tests pass.\n- Symbol comparison: both `.so` files export `encode_base64` (the only public function in `lib.h`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":208,"cache_read_input_tokens":23847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":208,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":45